{"id":"9cbc7fd5-55d9-47a0-b1f0-bc2ab87accde","revision":0,"last_node_id":25,"last_link_id":21,"nodes":[{"id":20,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-460,80],"size":[460,980],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Models & downloads","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"MarkdownNote"},"widgets_values":["## MODELS USED IN THIS WORKFLOW\n\n### Load Diffusion Model\n[⬇ Download krea2_turbo_bf16.safetensors · 26.3 GB](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_turbo_bf16.safetensors)\n\n*Place in: ComfyUI/models/diffusion_models*\n\n### Load CLIP\n[⬇ Download qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors · 8.9 GB](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors)\n\n*Place in: ComfyUI/models/text_encoders*\n\n### Load VAE\n[⬇ Download qwen_image_vae.safetensors · 254 MB](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_vae.safetensors)\n\n*Place in: ComfyUI/models/vae*\n\nThese three run the workflow as-is. The purple LoRA node ships **bypassed**, so you don't need\nanything else to hit Queue.\n\n### Optional — Realism Engine LoRA (the purple node, ships OFF)\n[⬇ Download Realism Engine for Krea 2 · civitai](https://civitai.com/models/3109006)\n\n*Place in: ComfyUI/models/loras, then enable the node: select it + **Ctrl+B**, or right-click →\nSet Mode → Always. Cleaner skin; every \"Realism Engine 0.4\" example was rendered with it on.*\n\n⚠️ After placing the files, restart ComfyUI or refresh model lists with the **R** shortcut.\n\n**Custom Nodes:** none — 100% ComfyUI core nodes.\n\n**Requirements:** Apple Silicon Mac. The bf16 UNet wants ~48 GB (peak ~26 GB). Low on RAM? Swap in `krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled` (~13 GB) — needs torch 2.11 + the ComfyUI-AppleSilicon-FP8 node (github.com/pawel-mazurkiewicz/ComfyUI-AppleSilicon-FP8). fp8 = less memory, same speed, same look."],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":21,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[40,80],"size":[420,1019.328125],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Recipe & Mac gotchas","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"MarkdownNote"},"widgets_values":["## RECIPE & MAC GOTCHAS\n\n**Locked recipe:** 8 steps · cfg 1.0 · euler · simple · denoise 1.0 — Krea's official distilled schedule.\nNegative = ConditioningZeroOut of the positive — at cfg 1 negatives are **dead**, don't write them.\n\n**Detail dial:** steps above 8 resolve extra micro-texture (skin pores, fabric weave) at\nproportional render time — 12-26 can be worth it on tight portraits. Same seed keeps\ncomposition across step changes, so hunt at 8 and re-render a keeper higher if it needs it.\n\n**MPS rules:**\n- `batch_size` MUST stay **1** (queue many *separate* jobs instead — that's fine). The batch_size WIDGET breaks on MPS: batch > 1 = mostly static frames + possible OOM\n- first render cold-loads ~26 GB, keep ComfyUI warm between renders\n\n**Prompting at cfg 1:** the positive prompt is the only steering. Lead with a photographic\nframing (`sharp high-detail realistic photograph, natural skin texture with fine pores` /\n`realistic candid iphone flash photo at night`) — NOT `amateur smartphone photo, unedited`,\nwhich actively softens. State the expression explicitly. Pin ethnicity/age or they drift when\nyou change any setting. `clear complexion, few freckles` cleans up freckle-heavy skin.\n\n**Realism Engine (purple node) — ships OFF (bypassed):**\n- **Enable with the mouse: right-click → Set Mode → Always** (or select it and press **Ctrl+B**).\n  Same keys toggle it back off. NEVER set strength to 0.0 on MPS — a zeroed LoRA NaNs the model\n  and renders pure black, so bypass instead of zeroing.\n- **0.4** is the sweet spot for clean skin. It doesn't fix freckles alone (use the prompt term);\n  above ~0.5 it drifts unpinned identity attributes.\n\n**TRAP - do NOT set the timestep shift manually.** Krea's model card lists shift (mu) 1.15,\nbut ComfyUI already applies it inside the krea2 loader. Adding a ModelSamplingSD3 node\n'per the card' double-shifts the schedule and renders pure colorful static."],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":1,"type":"UNETLoader","pos":[520,120],"size":[340,108],"flags":{},"order":2,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"unet_name","name":"unet_name","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"unet_name"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"weight_dtype","name":"weight_dtype","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"weight_dtype"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"MODEL","name":"MODEL","type":"MODEL","slot_index":0,"links":[1,16]}],"title":"Krea 2 Turbo (bf16)","properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.28.0","Node name for S&R":"UNETLoader"},"widgets_values":["krea2/krea2_raw_bf16.safetensors","default"],"color":"#232","bgcolor":"#353"},{"id":2,"type":"LoraLoaderModelOnly","pos":[520,260],"size":[435.78125,112],"flags":{},"order":7,"mode":4,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"model","name":"model","type":"MODEL","link":1},{"localized_name":"lora_name","name":"lora_name","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"lora_name"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"strength_model","name":"strength_model","type":"FLOAT","widget":{"name":"strength_model"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"MODEL","name":"MODEL","type":"MODEL","slot_index":0,"links":[]}],"title":"Realism Engine 0.4 (optional, ships OFF — Ctrl+B to enable)","properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.28.0","Node name for S&R":"LoraLoaderModelOnly"},"widgets_values":["krea2_realism_engine.safetensors",0.4],"color":"#323","bgcolor":"#535"},{"id":4,"type":"CLIPLoader","pos":[520,430],"size":[340,140],"flags":{},"order":3,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"clip_name","name":"clip_name","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"clip_name"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"type","name":"type","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"type"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"device","name":"device","shape":7,"type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"device"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"CLIP","name":"CLIP","type":"CLIP"